**7. Access and Owner Responsibilities.** Owner will:
(a) give Contractor access to the work area on working days from {work_hours_start} to {work_hours_end}, {work_days};
(b) provide water and electricity at the Property at no cost to Contractor;
(c) provide an equipment access path of at least {access_width} wide along {access_route}; Contractor may remove and replace these fence sections: {fence_sections}; replacement is to working condition, not new condition;
(d) show Contractor, before digging, the location of private underground lines not marked by public utility locates, such as irrigation, septic, drain lines, low-voltage lighting and propane lines; Contractor is not responsible for damage to private lines that were not shown;
(e) keep pets and children out of the work area, including open excavations, at all times;
(f) obtain HOA approval unless the Estimate says Contractor will apply for it;
(g) provide gate codes or keys: {access_instructions}; and
(h) respond to Contractor's questions within {owner_response_days} business days.
**Yard and driveway.** Heavy equipment can leave ruts in lawns and marks on driveways along the access path. Contractor will grade ruts smooth. Sod, landscaping and driveway repair are not included unless listed in the Estimate. Contractor will request public utility locates before digging.
